{
  "about": "Tiny Little Office journals (src/kit/share/journal.ts, backends/journal/, docs/crypto/journal.md). From a secret of 32 bytes: read = HKDF-SHA-256(ikm = secret, salt = empty, info = 'tinylittleoffice journal read v1' as UTF-8, 32 bytes); token = the same with info 'tinylittleoffice journal write v1'; id = the first 22 characters of base64url(SHA-256('tinylittleoffice journal id v1' as UTF-8 || read)); verifier = base64url(SHA-256(base64url(token) as UTF-8)), what the service keeps. An entry: plaintext = the content's JSON as UTF-8 after its length as 4 bytes big-endian, then zeros to a multiple of 256 bytes; c = AES-256-GCM(read, iv, plaintext, additionalData = 'tinylittleoffice journal v1' LF id LF seq LF kind, as UTF-8) with its 16-byte tag last; iv and c travel as base64url without padding, seq and kind in the clear. A writer's address is <service>/j/<id>#w<secret>, a reader's <service>/j/<id>#r<read>. Fixed secrets and IVs are for these vectors only: the site draws both from crypto.getRandomValues. Base64url here is RFC 4648's URL alphabet with '~' for 62 where the RFC has '-' (a hyphen is where a pasted link breaks a line), no padding; '-' is read as 62 too.",
